--- a/CHANGES
+++ b/CHANGES
@@ -1,5 +1,15 @@
 History of updates to Authen::SASL::Cyrus
 
+Unreleased
+Select Cyrus explicitly in tests and document backend selection with
+Authen::SASL 2.1700 and later.
+Preserve native pointer width in the connection typemap with sv_setref_pv
+and INT2PTR, following Russ Allbery's fix recorded in Authen::SASL::XS.
+Use STRLEN and I32 for Perl API output parameters, cast SASL callbacks to
+the library's generic function type, and free callback context before
+its table. Add interpreter context to cleanup for multiplicity builds.
+Test connection accessors, invalid objects and Perl callbacks through XS.
+
 0.13
 Updated the WRITE() method to use syswrite() and account for
 variable buffer sizes in SASL.
